IMPORT `euca-nouns`
IMPORT `euca-shared`

-- Section 208: self-employment assistance programs. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- A State may choose to pay an eligible individual's extended compensation as self-employment
-- assistance allowances, out of the individual's own account, for no more than 26 weeks together
-- with the program under section 4001(j) of the Supplemental Appropriations Act, 2008.
-- The relations: the State holds the power to set up the program (the individual is subject to it);
-- the individual holds the power to elect out at any time (the State is subject to that);
-- the State agency holds no duty to pay allowances unless it reasonably expects the individual
-- to be entitled to at least 13 times the weekly benefit amount (subsection (c)).
-- out of text: section 3306(t) of the Internal Revenue Code (the definition of a self-employment
-- assistance program, which subsection (b) adapts); section 4001(j) of and title IV of the
-- Supplemental Appropriations Act, 2008 (Pub. L. 110-252); "emergency unemployment compensation".
-- Judgment handed to the State agency (subsection (c)): "reasonable expectation" is taken as the
-- amount the State agency reasonably expects, a plain input.

§ `Section 208: self-employment assistance programs`

§§ `208(a)(1): the State's option, and who it reaches`

-- src:148 | At the option of a State, for any weeks of unemployment beginning after the date of enactment of this section [Feb. 22, 2012], the State agency of the State may establish a self-employment assistance program, as described in subsection (b), to provide for the payment of extended compensation as self-employment assistance allowances to individuals who would otherwise satisfy the eligibility criteria under this title.
@ref s 208(a)(1) (src:148)
GIVEN week IS A DATE
      `the State has established a self-employment assistance program under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual would otherwise satisfy the eligibility criteria under this title` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`extended compensation may be paid as a self-employment assistance allowance for the week` week `the State has established a self-employment assistance program under this section` `the individual would otherwise satisfy the eligibility criteria under this title` MEANS
        week GREATER THAN `22 February 2012`
    AND `the State has established a self-employment assistance program under this section`
    AND `the individual would otherwise satisfy the eligibility criteria under this title`

§§ `208(a)(2): paid from the extended compensation account`

-- src:149 | “(2) Subject to paragraph (3), the self-employment assistance allowance described in paragraph (1) shall be paid to an eligible individual from such individual’s extended compensation account, as described in section 202(b), and the amount in such account shall be reduced accordingly.
@ref s 208(a)(2) (src:149)
GIVEN `the amount in the extended compensation account` IS A NUMBER
      `the self-employment assistance allowance paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount in the extended compensation account after the allowance is paid` `the amount in the extended compensation account` `the self-employment assistance allowance paid` MEANS
    `the amount in the extended compensation account` MINUS `the self-employment assistance allowance paid`

§§ `208(a)(3): the combined eligibility limit`

-- src:151 | (A) Subject to subparagraph (B), for purposes of self-employment assistance programs established under this section and section 4001(j) of the Supplemental Appropriations Act, 2008 [Pub. L. 110–252, set out above], an individual shall be provided with self-employment assistance allowances under such programs for a total of not greater than 26 weeks (referred to in this section as the ‘combined eligibility limit’).
@ref s 208(a)(3)(A) (src:151)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the combined eligibility limit in weeks` MEANS 26

-- src:151 | (A) Subject to subparagraph (B), for purposes of self-employment assistance programs established under this section and section 4001(j) of the Supplemental Appropriations Act, 2008 [Pub. L. 110–252, set out above], an individual shall be provided with self-employment assistance allowances under such programs for a total of not greater than 26 weeks (referred to in this section as the ‘combined eligibility limit’).
