§§ `208(c): the 13 times test`

-- src:160 | “(c) In the case of an individual who is eligible to receive extended compensation under this title, such individual shall not receive self-employment assistance allowances under this section unless the State agency has a reasonable expectation that such individual will be entitled to at least 13 times the individual’s average weekly benefit amount of extended compensation and emergency unemployment compensation.
@ref s 208(c) (src:160)
GIVEN `the amount of extended compensation and emergency unemployment compensation the State agency has a reasonable expectation the individual will be entitled to` IS A NUMBER
      `the individual's average weekly benefit amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the individual may receive self-employment assistance allowances under section 208(c)` `the amount of extended compensation and emergency unemployment compensation the State agency has a reasonable expectation the individual will be entitled to` `the individual's average weekly benefit amount` MEANS
    `the amount of extended compensation and emergency unemployment compensation the State agency has a reasonable expectation the individual will be entitled to` AT LEAST
        (13 TIMES `the individual's average weekly benefit amount`)

